    "The power of Hidden Classes becomes even clearer when examining how modern CPU hardware interacts with system memory. Modern CPUs do not read single bytes from RAM; they fetch memory in sixty-four-byte cache lines. If an object's properties are scattered across disjointed memory locations via hash table buckets and linked lists, every property read forces the CPU cache controller to perform an expensive memory bus fetch, resulting in severe CPU pipeline stalls. By packing properties into fixed, predictable contiguous offsets dictated by Hidden Classes, V8 ensures that property accesses hit the ultra-fast L1 and L2 CPU caches.",
