    "Furthermore, V8 manages array elements using an entirely separate internal system called Elements Kinds. Just as named properties have hidden classes, array indices have elements kinds: Packed Smi (small integers), Packed Double, Packed Objects, and their corresponding Holey variants (arrays containing uninitialized holes). Once an array transitions from Packed Smi to Packed Double or Holey Elements, the transition is strictly one-way: V8 will never transition the array back to a more specialized elements kind. Maintaining packed, hole-free arrays ensures that numeric calculations run without redundant guard checks."
