    "In the Sweeping phase, memory pages containing only dead (white) objects are reclaimed immediately and added to free-list allocators. In the Compacting phase, V8 combats external memory fragmentation by relocating live objects on heavily fragmented pages into contiguous blocks on fresh pages. By scheduling incremental marking steps during event loop idle time and offloading heavy sweeping to background threads, V8 avoids the infamous multi-second garbage collection pauses that plagued early virtual machines, delivering smooth sub-millisecond tail latencies for enterprise Node.js microservices."
