    "This architectural bifurcation means that if your Node.js application performs heavy cryptographic hashing (such as bcrypt or crypto.pbkdf2) or large gzip compression tasks alongside filesystem operations, all of these tasks compete for the exact same four libuv worker threads! If four long-running cryptographic operations occupy all four workers, an incoming call to read a static HTML file or parse a critical JSON configuration file will be blocked in the threadpool queue. The main event loop remains idle, but the file read cannot progress until a crypto thread finishes.",
